<title>DENMARK: Danish May trade surplus 2.065 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish May trade surplus 2.065 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 2.065 billion crowns in May 1997, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>It compared to a revised 736 million crowns surplus excluding ships in April. Seasonally adjusted the surplus excluding ships was 1.667 billion crowns in May, compared to April's revised 1.378 billion crowns.</p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			   May 1997	April 1997    May 1996</p>
<p>Exports		    25.412	  27.131	  25.387</p>
<p>Imports		    23.173	  25.680	  21.335</p>
<p>Trade balance excl ships 2.065	    736	   3.839</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>balance excluding ships  1.667	   1.378	  3.454</p>
<p>NOTE - Eight analysts polled by Reuters forecast an average seasonally-adjusted May trade surplus excl. ships of 2.6 billion crowns. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969652</p>
